{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaZuJnU2wd69h3VxnvSg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rules were nested under `.filterForm .formField` in `reports.scss`, and they never matched because the reports app compiles its stylesheets as CSS Modules. Carbon's real class names (`cds--date-picker`, `cds--select`, `cds--date-picker__input`) are not in the module's scope, so CSS Modules hash the selectors into names Carbon never renders. The rules were deleted in PR #358 (commit `fbda030`). The commit's `.cds--` rules were removed, not rewritten, so the fix is deletion. I could not find a ticket key for this change.\n\n**Why they could never match**\n\n- The rules sat in `packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports.scss`, nested under `.filterForm` → `.formField`, and targeted `.cds--date-picker`, `.cds--select`, `.cds--select-input` and `.cds--date-picker__input` (lines 121–135 before the removal).\n- Commit `feb0ba00` states that each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class applies only when a component imports that stylesheet and uses it as `styles.<name>`. A plain `.cds--*` selector is therefore rewritten to a local hashed name. Carbon's DOM carries the unhashed global names, so nothing matches. The commit message is the only source for this mechanism; I did not open the build config to confirm it.\n- The one place the app handles a Carbon class correctly is `concept-search-results.scss`, which wraps it in `:global(...)`: `:global(.cds--skeleton__text)`.\n\n**What was done**\n\n- PR #358, commit `fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac` (\"chore: Remove inert Carbon CSS rules from reports app\", authored by solomonfortune, co-authored by Dennis Kigen), deleted the four `.cds--*` blocks. The `.formField` rule stayed.\n- Commit `feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198` (Dennis Kigen) is a related cleanup that removed 13 other unreferenced CSS Module classes. It does not touch the date-picker rules.\n\n**Ticket**\n\nNeither commit message nor the PR number carries a ticket key, and `search_commits` shows none for #358. I did not find the ticket that handled it. Commit `06a5b09` (#414) is a later layout change that also edits `reports.scss` and does not cite it either.\n\n**Evidence, best first**\n\n- `fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac` is the commit that removed the inert rules.\n- `packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports.scss` lines 115–120 show the `.formField` block as it now stands, after the removal.\n- `feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198` explains the CSS Module scoping that made the rules inert.\n- `packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/concept-search/concept-search-results.scss` lines 43–45 show the `:global(...)` form that does match Carbon classes.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-admin-tools\", \"commit\": \"fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-admin-tools\", \"pr\": 358},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-admin-tools/packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports.scss\", \"startLine\": 115, \"endLine\": 120},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-admin-tools\", \"commit\": \"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198\"},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-admin-tools/packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/concept-search/concept-search-results.scss\", \"startLine\": 43, \"endLine\": 45}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1274,"cache_read_input_tokens":34722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1274},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"500706d1-b9e5-438c-b1e5-edaa1ea1f2be","uuid":"1faaf8f5-4158-4c0d-b692-0b00c426bdaa","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:41:05.063Z","request_id":"req_011CgaZuJUNJeknrT